<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 6-mth T-bill av yield falls to 22.97 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 6-mth T-bill av yield falls to 22.97 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of six-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 22.97 at an auction on April 28 from 24.52 at the last auction on April 15, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					     Apr 28		 Apr 15</p>
<p> Series number		   KZ46K3010977	 KZ46K1610976</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)		 650		    580</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	     2,97		   2,67</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)		650		    580</p>
<p> Average price (pct)		    89.70		  89.08</p>
<p> Average yield (pct)		    22.97		  24.52</p>
<p> Tenor				   182 days	     182 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Oct 30, 1997     Oct 16, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
